@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@
+# Portable quiz contents
+
+Moderators use **Export** on a quiz to open a copyable JSON page, or **Import
+quiz** on `/moderate` to paste it into the **Quiz JSON** field and press **Import**.
+
+- `GET /moderate/quizzes/{id}/export` renders exactly one `<pre>` with pretty JSON.
+- `GET /moderate/quizzes/import` displays the form. POST to the same URL creates
+  a new quiz and redirects to its page. Matching titles never replace a quiz.
+- Both pages require moderator authentication; imports also require the existing
+  moderator CSRF token. No external services, uploads, or new dependencies.
+
+The only exported keys are `title` and `questions`; each question has `text`,
+`active`, and `options`; each option has `text` and `correct`. All flags are
+explicit booleans. There are no database IDs, positions, player answers, or other
+metadata. Every question is included, even inactive ones. Database ordering is
+used for both questions and options.
+
+Import requires objects at each level, strings for title/question/option text,
+and arrays for questions/options. Only `active` (default true) and `correct`
+(default false) may be omitted. Nulls, strings, and numbers are not coerced to
+booleans. Unknown keys are ignored on import and never carried into an export.
+A quiz may have zero questions, just like a newly created quiz.
+
+`src/questions.rs` provides the shared form/import validation and normalization:
+question text must be nonblank; there must be at least two nonblank options; at
+least one nonblank option must be correct. Multiple correct options are allowed.
+Text is trimmed and empty option rows are skipped without disturbing the order
+of surviving rows. An empty checked option does not satisfy the correct-answer
+rule. Inactive questions must still be valid.
+
+`src/contents.rs` uses separate transfer structs to prevent metadata leaking into
+exports. It parses and validates the entire input before opening a transaction,
+then inserts quiz/questions/options in one transaction. A validation error or
+failed database write cannot leave a partial quiz. Errors return HTTP 422 on the
+import page with the submitted JSON retained and question numbers in validation
+messages. Both the textarea and exported JSON are HTML-escaped, including text
+such as `</textarea>` or `</pre>`.
+
+Tests:
+
+```sh
+cargo test --offline --locked
+cargo clippy --offline --locked --all-targets -- -D warnings
+# With bin/serve running, and credentials exported if different from test defaults:
+python3 tests/transfer.py
+python3 tests/transfer_browser.py
+python3 tests/smoke.py
+python3 tests/browser.py
+python3 tests/persistence.py setup
+# Restart bin/serve with the same environment and storage directory.
+python3 tests/persistence.py verify
+```
+
+The HTTP regression first reproduced the missing Export link before
+implementation. Tests cover exact schema, ordered round trips, inactive
+questions, boolean defaults, duplicate titles, malformed and wrongly typed JSON,
+invalid later questions, atomic rollback on SQLite failure, hostile text,
+real-browser copying/error recovery, mobile layout, and restart persistence.
